docs {
  Hermes API collection (one folder per feature, D-070).

  Local run: start the stack (docker compose up), load the demo data (make demo) and get one token per role:
    TEST_TOKEN=$(make emulator-token ROLE=admin) ANALYST_TOKEN=$(make emulator-token ROLE=analyst) \
    READER_TOKEN=$(make emulator-token ROLE=reader) make bruno BRUNO_ARGS="--env-var demoMinItems=1"
  `token` is the admin's (it reaches every route); f13-6-auth checks 401 and 403 with the analyst and reader
  ones. Every operation of openapi/openapi.json has at least one request: each names it with an `operationId:`
  line in its docs, and tests/contract/test_bruno_coverage.py fails when one is missing. Requests read the
  current versions and ids first, so the collection runs again on the same installation. With demo data,
  demoMinItems=1 makes the data-dependent requests fail instead of skipping.
  In the Bruno app, paste the tokens into the `token`, `analystToken` and `readerToken` secrets of `local`.
}
